title: metarecord:remove-file
tags: [[GUI command]] Trash
kind: reference
summary: Remove the selected metarecord with a file: trash the file, or delete the metarecord only

The question <<cmd "metarecord:remove">> (the `Delete` key) asks of a metarecord
that has a file, in [[the command input|The command input]] — three ways out, where
an OK/Cancel dialog had two and Cancel deleted the metarecord:

|!Answer |!Does |
|`trash` — ''trash file'' |sends the file to the trash; its metarecord goes with it, restorable from the [[trash panel]] |
|`delete` — ''delete metarecord'' |keeps the file and deletes the metarecord alone (<<cmd "metarecord:delete">>, which confirms) |
|Escape |nothing |

`metarecord:remove-file trash` answers inline. Defined in the shipped `commands.js`
([[User commands]]), like `metarecord:remove`. See [[Sending files to the trash]].
